.TH SANCHALA-MIGRATE 1 "August 2026" "Sanchala OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sanchala-migrate \- Migration assistant for switching to Sanchala OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sanchala-migrate
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sanchala-migrate
helps users migrate from Windows, macOS, or other Linux distributions.
It imports user data, browser profiles, documents, and suggests
alternative applications.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Scan for data to migrate
.TP
.B import \fR[\fICATEGORY\fR]
Import data (documents, browsers, settings)
.TP
.B apps
Show application alternatives
.TP
.B status
Show migration progress
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-source \fIPATH\fR
Source partition or directory
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Show what would be imported
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output in JSON format
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message
.SH CATEGORIES
documents, browsers, email, music, photos, videos, settings
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Scan Windows partition:
.B sanchala-migrate scan --source /mnt/windows
.TP
Import browser profiles:
.B sanchala-migrate import browsers
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sanchala/migrate/
Configuration and app mappings
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rsync (1),
.BR sanchala-welcome (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Sanchala OS Team <dev@sanchala.id>
